WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.800
SIGNBRIDGE explores assisted communication in American Sign Language. This is a captioned walkthrough of real

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:11.600
application screens. The current release is a research interface, not a working ASL translator.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.800
Camera preview requires explicit activation. Short local videos can be played without upload. The walkthrough

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.000
shown here uses a prewritten suggestion. No model recognized a sign.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.400
The person can reject a suggestion and type a correction. Rejection does not invent a

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.800
meaning or silently accept the prediction. Text remains in the current page.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:38.000
The output contract and abstention policy are tested with synthetic data. That does not establish

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.200
recognition accuracy. There are no invented confidence scores or performance claims.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.600
A compatible licensed model, signer-disjoint evaluation and qualified ASL review are required. Signed replies need

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:54.000
authorized recordings of complete phrases. No such reply library is bundled yet.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
The project demonstrates accessible interaction, privacy controls and honest research boundaries. It is not a

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
replacement for an interpreter. The repository documents exactly what is available and what remains blocked.
